  "question": {
    "text": "For each positive integer <math><mi>n</mi></math>, let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>...</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msup></math>.&nbsp;If <math><mrow><mrow><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">lim</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>&#8734;</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo></math> then the value of <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;(where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is the&nbsp;greatest integer less than or equal to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>) is ____",
